<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Japanese group buys stake in Anglo CVRD bid.</title>
<headline>Japanese group buys stake in Anglo CVRD bid.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd said on Monday that a Japanese consortium headed by Nippon Steel has agreed to buy a ten percent interest in the Valecom Association, which is bidding for a stake in Brazil's soon-to-be privatised CVRD asset.</p>
<p>Valecom is made up of Anglo, Minorco and the Votorantim Group.</p>
<p>The news confirmed an earlier announcement released in Tokyo.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
